{"id": "EUVD-2026-93181", "enisaUuid": "58e2d786-b6ca-31de-8c16-1e96826a65de", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/ucma: Serialize join and leave on copy_to_user failure\n\nrdma_join_multicast() queues RoCE work that later reads the ucma_multicast\nthrough event->param.ud.private_data, then list_add()s the CMA multicast\nat the head of id_priv->mc_list. rdma_leave_multicast() matches only by\nsockaddr and destroys the first hit.\n\nucma_process_join() used to drop ctx->mutex after a successful join and\nretake it only if copy_to_user() failed. Two concurrent JOIN_MCAST calls\nwith the same address can therefore insert a second CMA entry before the\nfirst thread's leave. leave then cancels the newer work and the older\nworker still dereferences the ucma_multicast that the first thread frees.\n\nKeep ctx->mutex held from rdma_join_multicast() through copy_to_user() and,\non -EFAULT, through rdma_leave_multicast() so leave cannot miss this join.\nDo not leave if join itself failed: that path never published this address\non mc_list, and a leave-by-addr would destroy an earlier successful join.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:24", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29b9ed83d8bfab5c6e11fcbf1aa836aa4ae26cb9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/52172e11bd074ccaded21740ffeb67123f01dd00", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01e29d0d78a8f66f221625720a04939eef5ec1f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ae805d204cf1f15b87d1bf3529b4c649f3519420", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43c4e24bd10370fc976f6220518049ce71419399", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01cbdb724c584d7772fd25af2e4dfdf8527ce0d5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/83610ee5e498fa5bfcb80031d2b959baea276bf6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/662ade4de9ff5eceb0820a9f8e9fac70ba6a815b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98253", "GHSA-6rqw-4vwj-ww2r"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "15163246-c965-34d1-8530-6cfcd4ddc009", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "1eb34785-b4a2-30cf-bc40-a2e4c73bc087", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe454dc31e84f8c14cb8942fcb61666c9f40745b <52172e11bd074ccaded21740ffeb67123f01dd00"}, {"id": "338d2bbe-3b64-3b7b-a144-44c1233197ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "37691f14-15da-3306-acb2-347c68519462", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe454dc31e84f8c14cb8942fcb61666c9f40745b <43c4e24bd10370fc976f6220518049ce71419399"}, {"id": "44a663cc-0c50-3750-b2c8-5b8118c95f7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "63f3194b-6145-346b-9115-76f01dadf293", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe454dc31e84f8c14cb8942fcb61666c9f40745b <ae805d204cf1f15b87d1bf3529b4c649f3519420"}, {"id": "76e2fe46-0140-339b-811c-f9e8bb86ddcd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "85a3f4ae-c16c-38de-9ac7-92a9cfadd5bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "939bff7c-5392-3c7f-8aac-b898da5fc243", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe454dc31e84f8c14cb8942fcb61666c9f40745b <01cbdb724c584d7772fd25af2e4dfdf8527ce0d5"}, {"id": "bd07b970-9cdb-3fa1-a110-4c9e3a3253d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.11.3 <5.12"}, {"id": "c62e24bb-9220-36ae-9f77-ab12cfd0e844", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "c9627ac3-a041-33cc-81ea-38f86df0dfac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "cd346b47-352e-3b84-8e87-827af1b50878", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "e092e1d6-1d52-357d-9d55-ac8e65166072", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.20 <5.10.271"}, {"id": "e72fb1d8-598d-32a2-aed6-7a7b34220737", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe454dc31e84f8c14cb8942fcb61666c9f40745b <83610ee5e498fa5bfcb80031d2b959baea276bf6"}, {"id": "e9e87e87-ce36-3afc-b076-efbd0cef8edc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a3262b3884dd67b4c5632ce7cdf9cff9d1a575d4"}, {"id": "ed7a723e-47b8-3130-a266-48f37aa58ad7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "60d613b39e8d0c9f3b526e9c96445422b4562d76 <29b9ed83d8bfab5c6e11fcbf1aa836aa4ae26cb9"}, {"id": "f0c28e3d-757a-3edf-880c-a0c1131679c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe454dc31e84f8c14cb8942fcb61666c9f40745b <01e29d0d78a8f66f221625720a04939eef5ec1f6"}, {"id": "f1aff596-87f3-3437-beab-89409b748220", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.12"}, {"id": "f4f10d60-cea7-3fee-97e2-4289f0675a8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe454dc31e84f8c14cb8942fcb61666c9f40745b <662ade4de9ff5eceb0820a9f8e9fac70ba6a815b"}, {"id": "fcef07a3-0c35-3978-8944-f37656846502", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dd2e4694-8e47-3b4f-b93a-446866e35f27", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}